WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.621
Compute and time budget.

2
00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:05.699
Make a rough budget now, so the week doesn’t stall on infrastructure.

3
00:00:05.979 --> 00:00:23.259
Training a LoRA adapter on a few thousand short extraction examples on a 1 to 8 billion parameter model typically fits on a single rented or free-tier GPU within hours, especially with QLoRA (week 3); confirm on a small run before committing to the full one.

4
00:00:23.539 --> 00:00:37.320
Benchmarking needs the base and fine-tuned models served the same way, plus API calls for the frontier model: a few hundred test cases is cheap on any current API, but write the estimate down and set a spending cap.

5
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:41.611
Rented GPUs bill while running, so shut them down between sessions.

6
00:00:41.891 --> 00:01:00.131
A five-day shape that works: day 1, plan, license check, and test set frozen; day 2, training data built and verified, first small training run; day 3, full training run, dev-set checks, serving setup; day 4, the frozen benchmark for all systems, cost and latency measurement,

7
00:01:00.411 --> 00:01:06.832
failure analysis; day 5, the model card, the write-up, and a reproducibility check from a clean clone.

8
00:01:07.112 --> 00:01:13.277
Keep the lab 04 report format (lesson 10) from day 1, so results drop straight into it.
